# Article Drafting Workflow

Use this rule when creating a new article draft or running parallel agents for article work.

## Do

- Write new drafts into `/drafts/` unless the user explicitly instructs a production path.
- Give each parallel draft its own file or subfolder with a clear slug-like working name.
- Start from the reader question, the Canadian scope, the arithmetic to inspect, and the assumptions required.
- Include a short source checklist for any tax, contribution, threshold, policy, rate, or data claim.
- Mark unresolved facts as `TODO: verify` instead of filling them from memory.
- Keep draft status explicit: draft, needs source review, needs math review, or ready for human review.
- If a live calculator lets the reader apply the article, plan both shared call-outs (see `75-article-calculator-callout.mdc`).

## Do Not

- Do not publish, register, link from live hubs, or add a draft to sitemap/search unless explicitly instructed.
- Do not repurpose an existing live article slug for a different article concept.
- Do not let parallel agents edit the same draft file unless the user assigns a merge step.
- Do not treat an agent draft as final copy.
